title: TIKTOUK WordPress Credential Collection Toolkit - Batch Probe, Exposed File Harvesting and Hub Reporting
id: 336d459a-2bba-4f87-8e99-292b8fb23a2e
status: experimental
description: "Detects web request patterns attributed to the TIKTOUK WordPress credential-collection toolkit - malformed REST batch-route probes carrying the http://: path, UNION ALL SELECT payloads against WP_Query, fetches of the exposed configuration file set the collector pulls (wp-config.php.bak, .env, .git/config, backup.sql, wp-content/debug.log), and worker submissions to the toolkit hub endpoints /v1/ingest and /api/crack/report."
references:
  - https://www.levelblue.com/blogs/spiderlabs-blog/tiktouk-tracing-a-wordpress-credential-collection-toolkit
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-03
tags:
  - attack.t1595
  - attack.t1552
  - attack.t1555
  - attack.t1119
  - attack.t1071
logsource:
  category: webserver
detection:
  selection_batch_probe:
    cs_uri|contains:
      - 'http://:'
      - 'http%3A%2F%2F%3A'
  selection_sqli_payload:
    cs_uri|contains:
      - 'UNION ALL SELECT'
  selection_exposed_file:
    cs_uri|contains:
      - 'wp-config.php.bak'
      - '/.env'
      - '/.git/config'
      - 'backup.sql'
      - 'wp-content/debug.log'
  selection_hub_report:
    cs_uri|contains:
      - '/v1/ingest'
      - '/api/crack/report'
  condition: selection_batch_probe or selection_sqli_payload or selection_exposed_file or selection_hub_report
falsepositives:
  - Routine vulnerability scanners probing WordPress sites for exposed backup and environment files
  - Legitimate WordPress administration or migration tooling requesting the same backup files
level: medium
